1
00:00:00,531 --> 00:00:02,151
Sit down, traveller.

2
00:00:02,602 --> 00:00:06,324
One ticket, and my whole long story.

3
00:00:06,374 --> 00:00:09,985
I am the city you are riding into.

4
00:00:10,984 --> 00:00:14,005
The bazaar smells of frying and spice.

5
00:00:14,316 --> 00:00:18,848
Shah Jahan founded this capital in 1639;

6
00:00:18,898 --> 00:00:23,913
the Red Fort straddles this
bazaar's eastern fringe.

7
00:00:24,984 --> 00:00:29,830
Shah Jahan's daughter
Jahanara laid out this

8
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:34,607
street with its canal and moonlit pool.

9
00:00:34,914 --> 00:00:40,306
Tradition says the pool
named Chandni Chowk.

10
00:00:41,371 --> 00:00:44,052
Next, Chawri Bazaar.

11
00:00:44,365 --> 00:00:47,432
Above the stalls stands the Jama Masjid,

12
00:00:47,482 --> 00:00:52,103
finished in 1656 by about
five thousand workers.

13
00:00:53,153 --> 00:00:55,003
Still forward in time.

14
00:00:55,604 --> 00:00:58,037
At Patel Chowk, Jantar Mantar:

15
00:00:58,087 --> 00:01:05,788
an observatory of instruments for
measuring the heavens, finished in 1724.

16
00:01:06,748 --> 00:01:13,639
Forward, now. In 1931 the Viceroy
inaugurated this capital.

17
00:01:13,689 --> 00:01:20,361
Tens of thousands of labourers raised the
Viceroy's House, now Rashtrapati Bhavan.

18
00:01:21,339 --> 00:01:26,627
About half a million refugees came to me,
and many of my own left the other way.

19
00:01:26,677 --> 00:01:28,808
I remember canvas and dust.

20
00:01:29,815 --> 00:01:36,638
Malviya Nagar was one of the new
colonies for refugees: markets, schools,

21
00:01:36,688 --> 00:01:38,780
temples and gurdwaras.

22
00:01:39,819 --> 00:01:41,701
Here I turn the clock back.

23
00:01:42,517 --> 00:01:45,585
The train now comes up into daylight.

24
00:01:46,574 --> 00:01:55,792
Qutb Minar was begun around 1199 by Qutb
ud-Din Aibak and finished by Iltutmish,

25
00:01:55,842 --> 00:01:59,266
who made Delhi his capital.

26
00:02:00,213 --> 00:02:06,684
And beside it, an iron pillar from
the 5th century that resists rust.

27
00:02:06,734 --> 00:02:09,282
Phosphorus is the secret.

28
00:02:10,378 --> 00:02:16,780
[personal memory removed at the maker's request]
[personal memory removed at the maker's request]

29
00:02:17,407 --> 00:02:23,733
[personal memory removed at the maker's request]
[personal memory removed at the maker's request]

30
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:31,090
And this film? [personal memory removed at the maker's request]
[personal memory removed at the maker's request]

31
00:02:32,257 --> 00:02:38,871
A city of arrivals: colonies for those
who came, my own leaving the other way.

32
00:02:39,839 --> 00:02:42,081
Ride on, traveller.
